      "id": 53175,
      "name": "dypaca",
      "username": "dypaca",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dypaca/{size}/2079_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-02-18T03:00:29.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The official way is to have one player control two heros.&nbsp; Once you know the cards fairly well this isn't too difficult.</p><p>There is another suggestion on BGG here: <a href=\"http://www.boardgamegeek.com/thread/872326/my-journey-to-find-the-best-rules-for-a-2-players\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://www.boardgamegeek.com/thread/872326/my-journey-to-find-the-best-rules-for-a-2-players</a>.&nbsp; The basic idea is to play with H=3, two regular heros and one hero who starts incapacitated, but instead of using one incapacitated ability each player gets to use one on the incapacitated heros turn.&nbsp; It looks like the current version of that variant also suggests cycling which incapacitated hero to use each turn for some variety.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:27:17.359Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
